{
 "id": "trunk_passive_invivo.brownmcgill2008.braced_trunk_moment_angle_fit",
 "title": "Trunk moment-angle with abdominal co-activation (light/moderate/heavy brace) in flexion, extension, lateral bend",
 "layer": "property",
 "category": "trunk_passive_invivo",
 "subcategory": "active_trunk_stiffness",
 "region": "lumbar",
 "levels": [
  "lumbar (T12-sacrum / xiphoid-pelvis)"
 ],
 "condition": "abdominal co-activation ~5, 10, 15% MVC (ACTIVE muscle)",
 "quantity": {
  "name": "applied moment about L4/L5 vs normalised trunk angle",
  "definition": "exponential least-squares fit M = k exp(d*phi) to pooled trials and subjects; M = applied moment at L4/L5 (Nm), phi = trunk angle as % of max standing RoM; stiffness K = k d exp(d*phi) (Nm/%RoM). Moment-angle points given at 0-100% are computed from the fit (derived)",
  "unit": "Nm (coefficients as in data[].unit)"
 },
 "source": {
  "short": "Brown & McGill 2008",
  "authors": "Brown SHM, McGill SM",
  "year": 2008,
  "journal": "Clin Biomech 23:15-22",
  "doi": "10.1016/j.clinbiomech.2007.08.011",
  "n": 9,
  "sample": "9 healthy young males (university population)",
  "age": "23.9 (2.8) y",
  "sex": "9 M",
  "height_cm": 181,
  "weight_kg": 79.0
 },
 "protocol": {
  "summary": "Hips, knees and ankles secured on a fixed lower-body platform; upper body (arms, torso, shoulders) secured in a cradle gliding on nylon ball bearings over plexiglass (frictionless); right side-lying for flexion/extension, supine for right lateral bend. Experimenter pulled a cable perpendicular to the cradle at ~4-6 deg/s until no further rotation possible. Moment = force x moment arm from force application to the L4/L5 level. Angle: Isotrak source over sacrum and sensor over T12 (flexion/extension), source below ASIS level on lower abdomen and sensor over xiphoid (lateral bend); angle normalised to % of max RoM measured from upright standing. Relaxed = 'minimal activation' instruction; braced = abdominal co-activation to ~5/10/15% MVC at a right external-oblique biofeedback site; 14 EMG channels checked post hoc; 3 trials per condition, data pooled across trials and subjects.",
  "how_to_simulate": [
   "Posture: side-lying (flexion/extension) or supine (lateral bend), hips/knees/ankles fixed, upper body on a frictionless cradle (no gravity moment in the plane of motion)",
   "Impose lumbar flexion, extension or right lateral bend from neutral up to the model's maximum standing RoM; express angle as % of that max",
   "Activate abdominal muscles to the target %MVC (external oblique ~5/10/15%) with co-activation of the other muscles as the model's control allows, keep activation constant through the motion, and compute the external moment about L4/L5 required",
   "Compare M at each %RoM with the fitted curve; compare stiffness slope (Nm/%RoM)"
  ],
  "subject_model": {
   "sex": "M",
   "age": 23.9,
   "height_cm": 181,
   "weight_kg": 79.0,
   "disc_area_mm2": null,
   "source": "Methods 2.1 means"
  },
  "notes": "Fit pooled across subjects/trials (no between-subject SD). The extension curve has a large intercept k (12 Nm at 0%), i.e. a moment was needed to initiate motion. Max standing RoM values and peak moments are in Figs 5-7 (not digitised). ACTIVE condition: includes muscle short-range and reflex stiffness; never pool with passive tests."
 },
